## Context

Built during my internship at the Customer Assistance Center, PT Toyota-Astra Motor (2025-2026), to automate monthly reporting of customer surveys on education media (posters) across 38 car dealer branches.

## Problem

Survey responses arrived from Google Forms and were processed manually. For every dealer group, staff had to copy numbers from a pivot table, adjust month columns, recalculate survey rates, and export PDFs one by one, taking around 1 hour per cycle and risking inconsistent formatting.

## My role

Owner: I mapped the manual reporting steps, designed the 4-button guided workbook flow, and wrote the Excel VBA macros for data ingestion, deduplication, pivot synchronization, survey-rate calculation, and batch PDF export.

## As-is analysis

Reviewing the manual reporting cycle showed four repetitive, error-prone bottlenecks: duplicate survey submissions, shifting monthly columns in pivot tables, manual percentage calculations per dealer group, and repetitive one-by-one PDF page setup and export.

## Requirements

- Import new Excel or CSV survey exports while detecting and handling duplicates cleanly.
- Automatically refresh pivot tables and sync newly added month columns into summary sheets.
- Calculate monthly survey rates per branch and dealer group with visual flags for zero values.
- Export standardized one-page PDF reports per dealer group plus a consolidated all-dealer PDF.

## Solution design

I structured the workbook as a guided 4-step dashboard workflow (`Add Data` -> `Refresh` -> `Olah Data` -> `Export to PDF`) so any team member can run the monthly reporting cycle consistently without touching formulas or macros.

## Build

Built in Excel VBA with modular dashboard macros: `AddData` (array-based import, duplicate detection by Timestamp + survey date + branch, and chronological sorting), `RefreshSemuaPivot` and `SinkronkanSemuaData` (dynamic month column alignment), `OlahDataSurveyRate_Fixed` (branch binary scoring and dealer-group rate calculation with zero-value highlighting), and `ExportPDF_Dinamis_SatuHalaman` / `ExportPDF_SatuFile_BoldSaja_HinggaBulanTerakhir` (batch PDF generation). Source code (clean template with customer data removed): [github.com/thunderclouds863/excel-vba-survey-report-automation](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/excel-vba-survey-report-automation).

## Verification

Verified deduplication accuracy, monthly column syncing, dealer-group survey-rate formulas, and PDF pagination across all 38 branches against previously generated manual reports.

## Outcome

Cut a full survey report run from about 1 hour to 5-10 minutes while guaranteeing uniform formatting across every dealer-group PDF.

## Reflection

Turning a complex multi-sheet spreadsheet into four clearly labeled buttons made the automation immediately usable by non-technical teammates and eliminated formatting drift between monthly cycles.
